_GraphXY_ is a simple application where you can see graphs of functions of two variables.

$$z = f(x, y)$$

You can also compute gradient descent/ascent on the function.

$$ \dot{\mathbf{p}} = \alpha \nabla f(\mathbf{p}) $$


For a point $\mathbf{p}$, $\alpha \in [-1, 1]$ is a constant that determines whether it is gradient descent or ascent.

The `UI` accepts the usual syntax for defining functions. It supports the operators `+, -, *, /, ^` and functions such as `sin, cos, exp, tan, ln, ...`.

Feel free to download the program below.

![*GraphXY* app video](https://youtu.be/cjhTs1DJ4-k)

